I've had students end up with octal 240's in their source code files.
What happens is they use the ComposeCharacter key for Alt-S Save
commands or such, but dxnotepad then leaves the keyboard's compose
flag (and LED) set, so the next character or two that gets typed gets
mangled into something unrecognizable.  I use this as an argument that
they should be using Emacs (which handles the ComposeCharacter key
quite nicely) instead of dxnotepad...

