                      DECwrite Information Sheet

               DECwrite 2.0 Compound Document Software

            A Networkable Document Publishing Application

---------------------------------------------------------------------
Answering the Document Publishing Challenge
---------------------------------------------------------------------

The DECwrite(TM) document publishing application enables you to create 
and produce documents that combine text, tables, images, graphics, 
spreadsheet, and other application data.  These various forms of 
information can be drawn from multiple sources throughout your 
enterprise.  The DECwrite software also uses LiveLink(TM) connections 
and OLE* to your data sources to help keep documents up-to-date until 
the moment of distribution.

The premier product in Digital's CDA(TM) Suite of Publishing 
Applications, the DECwrite application allows you to exchange 
revisable DECwrite documents across different computing platforms and 
operating systems.  The DECwrite software works on VMS(TM) and 
ULTRIX(TM) RISC workstations (using the DECwindows(TM) Motif graphical 
interface), on Sun SPARCstations (using Motif), and on personal 
computers running the DOS operating system and Microsoft Windows 3.0 
or Windows 3.1.

Combining What-You-See-Is-What-You-Get (WYSIWYG) text processing with 
graphics creation, the DECwrite application lets you incorporate 
business graphics and data from other supported applications directly 
into DECwrite documents.

As a member of the CDA Suite of Publishing Applications, the DECwrite 
software complements the capabilities of other applications such as 
the DECimage(TM) scanning application, DECview3D for integrating CAD 
design snapshots, the DECwrite SGML Gateway for bi-directional 
CDA/SGML exchange, and DECpresent(TM) presentation graphics software.  
DECwrite software is a full participant in Digital's Network 
Application Support (NAS) architecture for integrating multivendor 
systems into your enterprise's distributed computing environment.

* Expected to be available in Summer 1992


---------------------------------------------------------------------
Highlights
---------------------------------------------------------------------
 
 ooo   WYSIWYG document creation, combining text, tables, graphics, 
     business charts, and images
 
 ooo   Full-feature word processing, including multiple-language 
     spell-checking and hyphenation, an online thesaurus, a 
     point-and-click function bar, and a mail-merge capability for 
     form letters
 
 ooo   Graphics support for illustrations and business graphics plus 
     image manipulation
 
 ooo   Color Encapsulated PostScript file support is included.
 
 ooo   Flexible publishing features including: modifiable style files, 
     automatic title numbering, automatically generated tables of 
     contents and indexes, and full-featured text formatting
 
 ooo   LiveLink connections and OLE* connections to supported 
     applications for up-to-the-minute charts, spreadsheets, images, 
     and other data
 
 ooo   Output options include Bookreader for online documentation and 
     PostScript for hard copy 
 
 ooo   Mail-merge capability for form letters
 
 ooo   VMS, ULTRIX RISC, Sun OS, and DOS operating systems
 
 
 * Expected to be available in Summer 1992

---------------------------------------------------------------------
Creates Documents Containing Text, Graphics, and Images across the 
Network
---------------------------------------------------------------------

The information needed to build a document is seldom in one place.  
Most often it exists on computers from different manufacturers in 
several locations across the network.  Pulling it all together 
requires a powerful system that integrates text, table, image, and 
graphics processing and can work with data formats from many vendors.  
The DECwrite document-publishing application lets you create documents 
based on up-to-date information in many forms from many sources across 
a heterogeneous network.

The DECwrite software runs under the DECwindows Motif graphical user 
interface on workstations running the VMS, ULTRIX RISC, or Sun OS 
operating systems and under Microsoft Windows 3.0 on personal 
computers running the DOS operating system. DECwrite also works in 
OpenLook-equipped Sun workstations in a Motif window. These graphical 
interfaces feature easy-to-learn and easy-to-use menus and icons and 
accept input for most functions from either the keyboard or the mouse.

In addition to its own editing interface, DECwrite software also 
supports keyboard interfaces for WPS-PLUS,(TM) WordPerfect,(TM) 
Microsoft(R) Word, EDT,(TM), EVE, and EMACS editors.  The DECwrite 
application can also import files created with these editors on other 
systems into DECwrite compound documents. The optional CDA Converter 
Library, the DECwrite SGML Gateway, and the ODA Gateway provide text 
and graphics conversion services to DECwrite. This versatility makes 
the DECwrite software an ideal complement to existing documentation 
systems.  


    ----------------------------------------------------------------
    Offers Advanced Word Processing Capabilities
    ----------------------------------------------------------------

The DECwrite application includes the word processing features you 
need to generate a wide range of documents.  Features include such 
functions as select, cut, copy, paste, undo, and redo.  The editor 
also supports sophisticated search and replace capabilities and 
advanced editorial features such as redlining, change bars, and change 
pages to support the needs of documentation and publication groups.

DECwrite contains a variety of writer's tools for interactive 
proofreading.  The American English version of the DECwrite software 
includes Houghton Mifflin's hyphenation routines, a dictionary based 
on the <American Heritage Dictionary,> usage alert, and an online 
thesaurus.  Users can control hyphenation according to local style or 
convention and maintain personal libraries of exceptions to the 
built-in dictionaries.  Spelling and hyphenation lexicons are 
available in multiple languages, and lexicons for specialized usages 
such as business and medical are available in American English.  

The DECwrite software supports multiple languages within one document.  
For example, you can combine Hebrew, French, German, English, and 
Japanese text in materials designed for an international market.  
Multi-language support includes hyphenation and optional spell 
checking for a variety of languages.

    
    ----------------------------------------------------------------
    Includes Powerful Graphical Editing Functions
    ----------------------------------------------------------------
    
The DECwrite document publishing application lets you combine text, 
graphics, and scanned images anywhere in the document.  You can link 
DECwrite documents to images scanned by the DECimage scanning 
subsystem and to images created with the DECpaint freehand drawing 
package.  An optional converter enables you to import TIFF images.  
The images can be positioned freeform or in frames and can be 
enlarged, reduced, annotated, scaled, or cropped to meet the goals of 
your current project.  

The DECwrite software includes an object-oriented graphics editor for 
creating vector line art and annotating illustrations.  You can use 
these capabilities to create organization charts, flowcharts, and 
other diagrams.  The graphics editor supports lines, polylines, 
squares, rectangles, polygons, circles, ellipses, and arcs.  Lines and 
object outlines can be solid, dashed, or dotted, and you can fill 
objects with a variety of patterns.  

Other graphics processing capabilities include freehand drawing, 
automatic alignment, object grouping, and scaling visually or by 
percentage.

In addition, the DECwrite application includes business graphics 
software for creating a variety of charts on VMS and ULTRIX RISC 
workstations.  The software includes several predefined chart styles, 
which you can modify, or you can create custom styles to fit your 
needs.  You can enter data directly into the worksheet or import it 
from Lotus(R) 1-2-3,(R) DECalc,(TM) DECalc-PLUS,(TM) DECgraph,(TM) 
DDIF,(TM) and ASCII files using a variety of optional converters.


    
    ----------------------------------------------------------------
    Supports a Wide Variety of Formatting Styles
    ----------------------------------------------------------------
    
The DECwrite application uses style files to define document format 
and page layout.  It includes more than 20 predefined style files for 
frequently used formats, i.e., memos, reports, technical documents, 
newsletters, etc. You can use these as-is, customize them, or create 
new ones.

The DECwrite software automatically paginates and numbers pages.  It 
also numbers text elements such as titles, section heads, paragraphs, 
lists, and footnotes.  Numbering can be numeric, alphabetic, or 
symbolic using characters such as bullets or dashes.  The DECwrite 
software also generates tables of contents and indexes automatically.  

Text formatting includes vertical and horizontal justification; ragged 
right, ragged left, and centered; widow and orphan control; variable 
leading; automatic cross referencing; side notes; support for the 
ISO-Latin I character set; and numeric or symbolic footnote 
references.


---------------------------------------------------------------------
Digital LiveLink and OLE* Connections Ensure Timely, Accurate 
Information
---------------------------------------------------------------------

LiveLink connections and OLE* connections simplify the task of 
ensuring that information drawn from other sources for use in DECwrite 
documents is always current.  These connections will automatically 
update the DECwrite document whenever the source information changes.  
Alternatively, you can choose to be notified that a change has taken 
place and decide at that time whether to include the updated 
information in the DECwrite project.

Using LiveLink and OLE* capabilities, you can create links between 
your DECwrite document and text, spreadsheet, chart, or image files 
created on other systems.  These capabilities help you produce reports 
and proposals that contain the most current information.  They also 
enable you to build entire books by creating LiveLink connections to 
multiple DECwrite documents, enabling authors working anywhere on the 
network to collaborate on documentation projects.

* Expected to be available in Summer 1992

---------------------------------------------------------------------
Automates Document Production
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Digital's line of PostScript(R) printers provide high-quality printed 
output of your DECwrite documents.  These printers include the LN03R 
ScriptPrinter, DEClaser 1150, DEClaser 2150, DEClaser 2250, the 
PrintServer(TM) 20, TurboPrintServer 20, PrintServer 40, and 
PrintServer 40 Plus high-performance network printer.  Additional 
print support includes the Apple LaserWriter II NT, and, for the DOS 
environment, the HP(R) LaserJet and selected non-PostScript printers 
via the DECprint(TM) Utility for PostScript to Sixel Printing for VMS.

Alternatively, VMS and ULTRIX RISC users can choose to export DECwrite 
documents into Bookreader to create online documentation that is 
easily and quickly accessible by multiple users.

----------------------------------------------------------------
Produces Fully Exchangeable Documents
----------------------------------------------------------------

Because DECwrite software is built upon the CDA architecture for 
compound documents, users can exchange documents though DECwindows 
Mail.  All LiveLink information is exchanged with the document; 
therefore, data is not lost.

The DECwrite software uses the DDIF document interchange format.  VMS 
and ULTRIX RISC versions include a two-way converter for DX(TM) and 
WPL; an ASCII converter; and WK1, DIF, CALC$GRD, and ASCII Tabular 
converters for importing data into DECchart.  The MicroSoft Windows 
version includes two-way Text, two-way WPL, and .BMP import 
converters. Other converters are available through the CDA Converter 
Library.


----------------------------------------------------------------
Digital Provides Full Service and Support
----------------------------------------------------------------

Digital's global presence assures you that service and support for 
your DECwrite solution are available worldwide.  With over 40,000 
service professionals at 450 locations in 64 countries, Digital is 
prepared to provide the services you need 24 hours a day, seven days a 
