    On Friday, I asked the question: 

>        We are in the process of buying VXT 2000 X-Terminals 
> from DEC.  But, we are having a problem deciding whether we
> should by the 17" or 19" terminals.  Since they both have the
> same resolution (1280 x 1024 pixels), it seems that the only
> difference is that the 17" might cause some eye strain.  Does
> anyone have any advice on this subject?

I received the following 4 replies:
   
  From:  Mark.Monger@Eng.Sun.COM (Mark Monger)

    I have both 16" and 19" Sony monitors in my office on my Sun's. I
    greatly prefer the 16". Seems to cause less eye strain for me.

  From:  COLOMBO@fndcd.fnal.gov (Rick 'VMS lives 4ever' Colombo)

    In my opinion, 17" is clearer (same number of pixels in less space), I          traded my 19" for the 17".  I guess it's smaller, but I don't notice it
    anymore.

  From:  "Michael C. Grant" <mcgrant@isl.stanford.edu>

    Put me down as one vote FOR a 19 inch terminal. It allows for big 
    fonts and big windows, plain and simple.


  From:  Steve Hespelt <fooz@sequoia.lle.rochester.edu>

           I asked my eye doc this question, he stated that it's not the 
           size of the object that you're reading, it's the distance from
           your eyes to the screen that really matters.

       | Did you eye doctor say if it made a difference if a person has to
       | sit closer to the monitor?  Also, do you have a preference to the
       | 17 or 19 inch size?

    He did say that the clearity of the characters made the biggest impact
    on the quality of vision.  The 17" screens on our Suns here seem to be
    crisper than my Tek XP27 w/19" screen.  If I had to choose, I'd go with
    the 17" screen based soley on the quality of the characters.  My eye
    doctor recommended focusing on something >30 feet away every 20-30
    minutes for > 1 minute at a time.  Hope this helps.


  -----------------------------------------------------------------

     Based on these replies, it seems that the most important question
is whether the clarity of the characters is better on the 17 or the
19 inch monitors.  Rick Colombo has used both monitors and reports
that the 17" monitors have better character clarity.  Also, the
respondents have voted 3-1 in favor of the 17" monitor, so I guess the
17" monitors win.

     The only concern I have left is that since the user has to sit
closer to the 17" monitors, they may be receiving more of the photons
that are being emmited by the monitor.   But, there is probably no
scientific data to support this claim.

     Thanks to all who responded.

        Erik Eilerts
        University of Texas at Austin
        eilerts@cs.utexas.edu 


