One question has anyone ever seen a truly secure computer case?
I mean the cases on Personal Computers are a piece of cake to
remove even if they have a built in lock.  And that's before
you get fancy and actually start dealing with the lock, not the
way it catches.

Assuming that the way the lock is set up to keep the case closed
is fairly good, you have to realize there are a lot more people
in this world that understand the problems with locks than you
really want to think about.

Even if the lock is fairly good, a determined person can STILL
get into the case, and not attract too much attention while
doing it.

It makes more sense to secure sensitive equipment and data, and
implement means to easily and quickly clean up machines in the
open, than making every machine a fortress unto itsself.

