Message-ID: <k2.704099281@woodstock>
Summary: DELQA could be updated to a DELQA Plus 
Lines: 23

Some time ago I've installed a second ethernet interface in my Microvax.
The new device was a DELQA-YM (DELQA Plus). I've did a look on both
boards, and my intentetion was, that the DELQA-YM did only differ
in the ROM'S to the older DELQA.

I've now tried to copy the ROM's and gee it works !

So if you have access to the DELQA-YM ROM's and to a ROM burner,
you could upgrade all your DELQA's. Especially on short packets,
the DELQA in the Plus Mode is significantly faster. (4-times as
the doku says!). You will need two 27128 EPROM's (128 kbit or 16k * 8)
Access time isn't critical (300 ns should work).

Sincerely,
Klaus Steinberger

P.S. To prevent misunderstandings: This will not work with the DEQNA!
     The very old DEQNA is significantly different to DELQA's.
