I am afraid to be the bearer of bad news, however, if any SCSI 
controllers are compatible with PDP-11 systems, they will most 
likely emulate DEC MSCP controllers. This means that a different 
device driver will be required. While technically speaking there 
is no need to do a complete SYSGEN, you will need to access a 
variety of files which are on the normal distribution disks.
 
Assuming that the controllers mimic an MSCP device, bootstrapping 
should not be too difficult, providing that your bootstrap PROMS 
"know" about MSCP devices.

