> 1. Missing fonts for remote X-clients.  If I e.g. run a DECTERM
>     from either a VAX or a DECstation, then there are messages
>     from the client that it is unable to locate fonts (e.g. the
>     menu font families).  Does anybody have a set of font alias
>     files and instructions about what to do with them to
>     make these messages go away?

Take the VMS file SYS$COMMON:[SYSHLP.EXAMPLES.DECW]FONTS.ALIAS in the
fonts directory on the ELC. It will convert almost all the fancy VMS
fonts into standard X11 ones. Just copy it as fonts.alias (in $FONTPATH)
and restart your server (or xset fp default).

