Actually, an easier way ...you don't have to take it apart. All you have
to do is hit the power switch. When you turn it back on it will try to auto-
boot back to multi-user mode. Since the file system is "dirty" it will
have to fsck all the partitions. We have had an ~80% success rate that 
one of the partitions is corrupt enough that it will fall back
into single user mode with a message of "please fsck by hand".

