We just received approval to setup a Macintosh 10-base-T network and would
like various opinions, suggestion, likes, dislikes etc....

To give a some background on our network and what we plan to do follows:

	We will be running a PS/2 Model 80, which will be running Netware
	3.11 (using the Macintosh NLM) as our Macintosh Server,

	Our PC Network is running Token-Ring and our Sun's and VAX are
	connect to Ethernet.  We have a CISCO to bridge the Token-Ring
	and Ethernet worlds.  We also have Pathworks for VMS on our VAX
	to allow for VAX to MAC connectivity.

	We would like to share all of our printers (if possible) no
	matter if they are Netware, Apple or VAX.

	We also would like a hub which supports SNMP agents for great
	network management over the WAN (if possible).

