Hi everyone,

	yesterday, i had posted a disperate help message to read
	input from a digitizier on a DECstation 5000, the digitizier
	was GTCO, 4 x 5 feet. My question was whether I was reading
	the correct /dec/tty** dev. driver to get to the Digitizier?
	And also the method. I must give my thanks to:

From: Stefan Manke <manke@ira.uka.de>
From rogerhef@matt.ksu.ksu.edu Tue Apr  7 08:15:52 1992

	Stefan, sent me a piece of code , from which we realized our mistake.
	Basically, from the developers standpoint, Victory was over
	different flavors of UNIX and UNIX-boxes. The initial code
	was working on the Sun, but on the DECstation, we realized later
	was working only with -POSIX complilation option. DEC box has 3 option
	to set ioctl calls, standard ultrix, POSIX, System V. Here are the
	summaries, and our kludge.
thanks
cosc4hf@menudo.uh.edu
