problem using other OS's X-servers as long as they speak your language, that 
means X and one of the transports above.

>4) Are there any special issues that have to be addressed in porting an
>XLib-based program from Unix to VMS?

Not that I now of except for the usual things of porting normal "C" programs to 
the VMS platform (file system stuf etc.) X-wise there's no difference. There 
are people who ported the Athena widget set to VAX/VMS. I ported many programs 
published in comp.sources.x to VAX/VMS. (example: XV)

