des@frogland.inmos.co.uk (David Shepherd) writes:
>when applying formal methods to the t800 fpu ucode i found a bug that
>could only have been found by testing by evaluating
>	(x * 0) + y, where abs(y) < abs(x)
>how long 'till a random code sequence gets that?

Right. I recall a program that was extensively machine-tested, using
randomly generated parameters. In spite of this, the first real user
promptly crashed it. They'd forgotten that most random number
generators are tuned to never generate a zero.

On the other hand, static methods often incorporate incorrect
assumptions, a common one being that the tools are bug-free.

When practical, use *all* test methods.
