Greg,

 No worries. There's no reason you "should" know it. Actually, you can set
a boot path to any SCSI Host Adapter on the system. The variation would be
in the option number of the boot path:

	>>boot 3/rz0/vmunix -a

will boot off of SCSI device 0 on TURBOchannel option 3, which on the 
DS5000/240 happens to be where the I/O CTL is that runs the motherboard SCSI.
But, if you wanted to put a PMAZ-AA in the slot directly above the motherboard
SCSI port (which is slot 0), it would be:

	>>boot 0/rz0/vmunix -a


  As for when an "upgrade" will be available, I'll assume you're asking
about when a TURBOchannel SCSI Host Adapter option will be available that
does support DMA. There are two SCSI adapters that are being designed internal
to DEC and both of them do DMA. I'll have to ask Product Management what they
want said about availability.

  There are also two external designs that both include DMA. I'll see if I
can get them to allow us to post an update as well. But, there are solutions
coming.

I hope that this helps.

				Thanx,
